WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.000
Activity program.

00:02.000 --> 00:08.000
♪♪

00:10.000 --> 00:12.000
♪♪

00:12.000 --> 00:24.000
Applause

00:24.000 --> 00:29.000
Thank you, thank you very, very much ladies and gentlemen, and welcome to our show.

00:29.000 --> 00:35.000
You know, I just went through the penalty of being a celebrity.

00:35.000 --> 00:40.000
You see, this being a studio, you know where stars come in and go actors, you see,

00:40.000 --> 00:47.000
there's always a crowd of people outside clamoring for autographs and souvenirs and everything.

00:47.000 --> 00:53.000
And just as I was coming in, a little old lady walked over to me with a pair of scissors in her hand,

00:53.000 --> 00:59.000
and before I knew what she was doing, she cut off the end of my tie.

01:01.000 --> 01:09.000
And you know, the whole thing was so unnecessary, I kept telling her I'm not Rock Hudson.

01:13.000 --> 01:18.000
But you know, normally, of course, people just ask for autographs, that's all.

01:18.000 --> 01:23.000
And of course, sometimes they ask you to sign the silliest thing, a little piece of cardboard.

01:23.000 --> 01:27.000
Well, there was a fellow standing there tonight who handed me a dollar bill,

01:27.000 --> 01:29.000
you know, wanted me to put my name on it.

01:29.000 --> 01:33.000
And all those ridiculous, I decided to get a dollar bill.

01:33.000 --> 01:36.000
I think it was a dollar.

01:38.000 --> 01:40.000
No, it was five.

01:41.000 --> 01:44.000
Now at least I can pay for my tie.

01:44.000 --> 01:49.000
But I, and you know a strange thing, you've probably heard this a million times,

01:49.000 --> 01:52.000
about people who ask for autographs.

01:52.000 --> 01:57.000
For some reason or other, they're always ashamed to say it's for themselves.

01:57.000 --> 02:02.000
Everybody, they always say it's for my granddaughter or my grandson, you know.

02:02.000 --> 02:06.000
I don't know why it is, but they're ashamed to say, give me an autograph for me,

02:06.000 --> 02:08.000
it's for my granddaughter, they always do it.

02:08.000 --> 02:13.000
But then, of course, don't get me wrong, I appreciate autographs.

02:13.000 --> 02:15.000
I appreciate all of my fans.

02:15.000 --> 02:19.000
As a matter of fact, so much so, that tonight I've gotten so many lovely fan letters,

02:19.000 --> 02:23.000
I'd like to read some of them for you tonight, if you don't mind.

02:23.000 --> 02:26.000
Could I have my fan mail, please?

02:28.000 --> 02:29.000
Thank you.

02:32.000 --> 02:35.000
I'm not going to be able to read it all, you know.

02:35.000 --> 02:40.000
I'll just, oh for heaven's sake, this isn't my bag.

02:40.000 --> 02:43.000
It's Don Wilson's lunch.

02:47.000 --> 02:50.000
There's something moving in there, I don't know what.

02:50.000 --> 02:52.000
Here, take this back, will you please?

02:52.000 --> 02:56.000
For heaven's sake, imagine having one.

03:01.000 --> 03:04.000
You thought I was kidding, didn't you?

03:04.000 --> 03:08.000
Get this out of here, he has to eat it later.

03:08.000 --> 03:10.000
Here, here.

03:13.000 --> 03:17.000
But anyway, ladies and gentlemen, the reason that I wanted you to read,

03:17.000 --> 03:20.000
I wanted to read some of these fan letters to you,

03:20.000 --> 03:24.000
is because you'd be surprised how many letters I get asking me

03:24.000 --> 03:29.000
if just once I would play a violin solo and finish it,

03:29.000 --> 03:31.000
that I'd stop kidding around with it, you see.

03:31.000 --> 03:34.000
So I'm going to do it, because they want me to.

03:34.000 --> 03:38.000
I'm going to do it now.

03:41.000 --> 03:44.000
May I have my violin, please?

03:46.000 --> 03:47.000
Thank you.

03:47.000 --> 03:49.000
My bow.

03:49.000 --> 04:01.000
And my rosin.

04:08.000 --> 04:12.000
And of course,

04:12.000 --> 04:17.000
my bow.

04:17.000 --> 04:21.000
Normally, you see, I would have a stage hand to bring these things out,

04:21.000 --> 04:27.000
but I just thought I'd like to do something for you folks who are not music lovers.

04:30.000 --> 04:32.000
You may go.

04:32.000 --> 04:38.000
This bit, this bit alone, cost me $600.

04:38.000 --> 04:43.000
But it started three beautiful friendships.

04:43.000 --> 05:06.000
And now, ladies and gentlemen, I would like to play Monty's Charters.

05:13.000 --> 05:22.000
Did you come up from the audience?

05:22.000 --> 05:27.000
Well, honey, you're not supposed to come up here on the stage in the middle of a show, you know.

05:27.000 --> 05:31.000
I'm sorry, Mr. Benny, but I thought maybe you'd let me have your autograph.

05:31.000 --> 05:34.000
Well, I'll give it to you as soon as the show is over.

05:34.000 --> 05:37.000
Just go back and come back later.

05:37.000 --> 05:39.000
Oh, wait a minute, as long as you were here.

05:39.000 --> 05:42.000
Come here, I'll give it to you now.

05:42.000 --> 05:44.000
You sure this autograph is for you?

05:44.000 --> 05:47.000
I mean, it isn't for your grandmother or anything?

05:47.000 --> 05:48.000
Oh, no, this is for me.

05:48.000 --> 05:51.000
My grandmother already has the end of your tie.

05:56.000 --> 05:58.000
I see. All right.

05:58.000 --> 06:00.000
Then I will give you this autograph.

06:00.000 --> 06:02.000
What is your name, honey?

06:02.000 --> 06:03.000
Tony Marcus.

06:03.000 --> 06:05.000
Tony, Tony Marcus.

06:05.000 --> 06:06.000
That's a cute name, isn't it?

06:06.000 --> 06:08.000
Oh, wait a minute, this is so uncomfortable.

06:08.000 --> 06:10.000
Here, hold this a minute, will you, darling?

06:10.000 --> 06:12.000
Be careful, that's a violin here.

06:12.000 --> 06:16.000
Here, hold the bow. Don't touch the hair or anything.

06:16.000 --> 06:20.000
Just hold the bow, and I'll write something nice on here, you know.

06:20.000 --> 06:25.000
To Tony, with all good wishes.

06:25.000 --> 06:28.000
With all good wishes.

06:31.000 --> 06:34.000
Thank you, thank you very much. That's fine.

06:34.000 --> 06:37.000
No, no, that's fine, honey. That's fine.

06:37.000 --> 06:40.000
That's fine.

06:40.000 --> 06:43.000
Give me the violin already.

06:52.000 --> 06:54.000
Now, go back where you were sitting.

06:54.000 --> 06:55.000
I'll see.

06:55.000 --> 06:57.000
Wait a minute, come here.

06:57.000 --> 06:59.000
Here's the autograph. You can iron it out.

06:59.000 --> 07:01.000
Wait a minute.

07:01.000 --> 07:03.000
I probably, you know, I was a little bit upset.

07:03.000 --> 07:07.000
You're welcome. You're welcome.

07:07.000 --> 07:12.000
Of course, it would be ridiculous for me to play that same number now.

07:12.000 --> 07:15.000
But ladies and gentlemen, I know you won't be disappointed

07:15.000 --> 07:18.000
when I introduce my guest star of the evening.

07:18.000 --> 07:21.000
A very, very talented, lovely young lady,

07:21.000 --> 07:24.000
who is one of our most popular recording stars,

07:24.000 --> 07:33.000
and certainly one of our most beautiful, Miss Julie London.

07:39.000 --> 07:42.000
Hey, Daddy.

07:42.000 --> 07:48.000
I want a diamond ring, bracelets, everything.

07:48.000 --> 07:55.000
Daddy, you ought to get the best for me.

07:55.000 --> 08:04.000
Daddy, gee, won't I look swell in this saver's clothes with all those labels?

08:04.000 --> 08:13.000
Daddy, you ought to get the best for me.

08:13.000 --> 08:21.000
Here's an amazing revelation with a bit of stimulation.

08:21.000 --> 08:25.000
I'd be a great sensation.

08:25.000 --> 08:29.000
I'd be your inspiration.

08:29.000 --> 08:37.000
Daddy, I want a brand new car, champagne, caviar.

08:37.000 --> 08:44.000
Daddy, you ought to get the best for me.

08:44.000 --> 09:11.000
For occasional recreation, how about San Juan for vacation?

09:11.000 --> 09:19.000
I promise I will ration all you need for relaxation.

09:19.000 --> 09:27.000
Daddy, I want some charge accounts at Saks for large amounts.

09:27.000 --> 09:34.000
Daddy, you ought to get the best for me.

09:34.000 --> 09:41.000
You ought to get the best for me.

09:41.000 --> 09:47.000
Oh, baby, if you can't make it, I'm going to have to split it.

09:47.000 --> 09:50.000
You dig?

09:50.000 --> 10:11.000
Bye.

10:11.000 --> 10:16.000
Julie, that was just wonderful, and I can't tell you how happy I am that you're on the show with me.

10:16.000 --> 10:21.000
Oh, well, Jack, it's a big thrill for me working with America's number one comedian.

10:21.000 --> 10:23.000
What'd you say, Julie?

10:23.000 --> 10:28.000
I said it's a big thrill for me to be working with America's number one comedian.

10:28.000 --> 10:32.000
Look, Julie, when you sing, whisper, you see?

10:32.000 --> 10:41.000
But when you're complimenting me, speak up.

10:41.000 --> 10:46.000
I mean, the way she talks, I feel like we're doing our show in a library.

10:46.000 --> 10:49.000
But anyway, Julie, I do want to thank you for the compliment.

10:49.000 --> 10:55.000
I've always been a great admirer of yours, you know, and I love all of the albums that you make.

10:55.000 --> 10:57.000
You do such a good job with them.

10:57.000 --> 10:59.000
Oh, that's very nice of you to say so, Jack.

10:59.000 --> 11:02.000
And the records, so many of those records.

11:02.000 --> 11:07.000
Tell me, what is the most difficult thing about making a record album?

11:07.000 --> 11:11.000
Posing for the covers.

11:11.000 --> 11:15.000
I want to tell you that not only that I'm glad that you're on the show,

11:15.000 --> 11:17.000
this is the second time you've been with me.

11:17.000 --> 11:18.000
Oh, I should say so, Jack.

11:18.000 --> 11:22.000
And, you know, I always enjoy being with you so much.

11:22.000 --> 11:23.000
You have?

11:23.000 --> 11:25.000
Mm-hmm. I certainly do.

11:25.000 --> 11:27.000
You're so easy to work with.

11:27.000 --> 11:31.000
Usually I'm nervous, but with you I'm so relaxed.

11:31.000 --> 11:35.000
You make everyone feel so comfortable, so at ease.

11:35.000 --> 11:37.000
Really?

11:37.000 --> 11:44.000
I've admired you for so long that I think you're the sweetest person I know.

11:44.000 --> 11:48.000
You're whispering again.

11:48.000 --> 11:50.000
Well, I mean, you are sweet.

11:50.000 --> 11:53.000
Wait for the laugh, honey. Wait for the laugh.

11:53.000 --> 11:54.000
What did you say?

11:54.000 --> 11:55.000
I mean it, Jack. I mean it.

11:55.000 --> 11:58.000
You're very sweet. I see.

11:58.000 --> 12:00.000
And, you know, I'd really like to tell you what I think of you,

12:00.000 --> 12:03.000
but maybe you'd let me sing it to you, huh?

12:03.000 --> 12:06.000
You want to sing what you think? Okay, go ahead.

12:06.000 --> 12:20.000
Whenever I'm downhearted or have a trying day,

12:20.000 --> 12:25.000
you come along and ease me.

12:25.000 --> 12:29.000
You're sweet that way.

12:29.000 --> 12:37.000
And when I'm feeling moody, without a word to say,

12:37.000 --> 12:40.000
you lighten my mood.

12:40.000 --> 12:43.000
And I'm open.

12:43.000 --> 12:47.000
You're sweet that way.

12:47.000 --> 12:54.000
And any time I want some more affection,

12:54.000 --> 13:03.000
I merely hold my breath.

13:03.000 --> 13:14.000
I feel, I feel alive when things are not okay

13:14.000 --> 13:19.000
because you never let me down.

13:19.000 --> 13:48.000
I'm sweet that way.

13:48.000 --> 13:49.000
Isn't she beautiful?

13:49.000 --> 13:52.000
I think she likes me, too, you know.

13:52.000 --> 13:57.000
And now, ladies and gentlemen, not to disappoint you,

13:57.000 --> 13:59.000
I'm going to do what I started to do before,

13:59.000 --> 14:01.000
and that is play a violin number.

14:01.000 --> 14:02.000
Now, all the way through.

14:02.000 --> 14:08.000
Could I have my violin, please?

14:08.000 --> 14:12.000
My bow.

14:12.000 --> 14:26.000
And now my rosin.

14:26.000 --> 14:29.000
Where is that third girl that was here?

14:29.000 --> 14:31.000
That was me.

14:31.000 --> 14:32.000
You?

14:32.000 --> 14:33.000
Yeah.

14:33.000 --> 14:38.000
I didn't know I had to come back, so I took my makeup off.

14:38.000 --> 14:44.000
Oh, get off of here, will you?

14:44.000 --> 14:47.000
That's the most ridiculous thing you'll ever hear.

14:47.000 --> 14:49.000
And now, ladies and gentlemen, I'm going to play

14:49.000 --> 15:15.000
the meditation from Thais.

15:15.000 --> 15:17.000
I'm sorry to bother you, but on this autograph you gave me,

15:17.000 --> 15:20.000
you spelled Tony wrong.

15:20.000 --> 15:22.000
I spelled Tony wrong?

15:22.000 --> 15:23.000
Yes.

15:23.000 --> 15:26.000
When Tony is a girl's name, it's spelled with an I.

15:26.000 --> 15:28.000
Oh, and I spelled it with a Y.

15:28.000 --> 15:33.000
No, with an E.

15:33.000 --> 15:34.000
I spelled Tony with an E?

15:34.000 --> 15:37.000
Yes, two of them.

15:37.000 --> 15:39.000
Oh, for heaven's sake.

15:39.000 --> 15:42.000
Well, look it, I'll fix it up for you later, huh?

15:42.000 --> 15:45.000
And Mr. Benny, I'm sorry I interrupted you

15:45.000 --> 15:47.000
because I love to hear you play the violin.

15:47.000 --> 15:48.000
Do you really?

15:48.000 --> 15:50.000
Yes, I listen to you all the time.

15:50.000 --> 15:51.000
No.

15:51.000 --> 15:55.000
Yes, and you know that number you did with Giselle McKenzie?

15:55.000 --> 15:58.000
Oh, you heard, the one that, Getting to Know You?

15:58.000 --> 16:00.000
Uh-huh, I can play that.

16:00.000 --> 16:01.000
Really?

16:01.000 --> 16:03.000
I always practiced it at home.

16:03.000 --> 16:05.000
You mean after you saw Giselle?

16:05.000 --> 16:06.000
Me, after you heard us do it, huh?

16:06.000 --> 16:07.000
Yes.

16:07.000 --> 16:08.000
Oh, for heaven's sake.

16:08.000 --> 16:09.000
And you can play it?

16:09.000 --> 16:10.000
Uh-huh.

16:10.000 --> 16:11.000
Her part?

16:11.000 --> 16:12.000
Yes.

16:12.000 --> 16:13.000
Oh, gosh, yeah.

16:13.000 --> 16:15.000
Would you like to play it with me?

16:15.000 --> 16:16.000
All right.

16:16.000 --> 16:17.000
You wouldn't be nervous or anything, would you?

16:17.000 --> 16:18.000
No.

16:18.000 --> 16:19.000
You sure?

16:19.000 --> 16:20.000
All right, here, hold it.

16:20.000 --> 16:21.000
I'll get another violin.

16:21.000 --> 16:25.000
Oh, Don, Don, will you please get me a violin from the orchestra?

16:25.000 --> 16:27.000
You sure you won't be afraid?

16:27.000 --> 16:28.000
No.

16:28.000 --> 16:57.000
Well, for a fella that eats his lunch out of a mail bag,

16:57.000 --> 16:58.000
he's got beautiful legs.

16:58.000 --> 16:59.000
Oh, by the way, you know, I used to have a lot of trouble with Giselle McKenzie

16:59.000 --> 17:00.000
when we played that number.

17:00.000 --> 17:01.000
See, she used to show off and do a lot of tricks and everything to upset me, see?

17:01.000 --> 17:02.000
So don't, just play the counter melody, just straight, no tricks or anything, huh?

17:02.000 --> 17:03.000
You promise?

17:03.000 --> 17:04.000
Yes.

17:04.000 --> 17:05.000
You won't show off with it or anything like she did, just straight, huh?

17:05.000 --> 17:06.000
You know, it's a beautiful counter melody, no tricks.

17:06.000 --> 17:07.000
All right, let's tune up.

17:07.000 --> 17:08.000
Give me A, will you please?

17:08.000 --> 17:09.000
A.

17:09.000 --> 17:10.000
A.

17:10.000 --> 17:11.000
A.

17:11.000 --> 17:12.000
A.

17:12.000 --> 17:13.000
A.

17:13.000 --> 17:14.000
A.

17:14.000 --> 17:15.000
A.

17:15.000 --> 17:16.000
A.

17:16.000 --> 17:17.000
A.

17:17.000 --> 17:18.000
A.

17:18.000 --> 17:19.000
A.

17:19.000 --> 17:20.000
A.

17:20.000 --> 17:21.000
A.

17:21.000 --> 17:22.000
A.

17:22.000 --> 17:23.000
A.

17:23.000 --> 17:24.000
A.

17:24.000 --> 17:25.000
A.

17:25.000 --> 17:30.000
A.

17:30.000 --> 17:31.000
That's close enough.

17:31.000 --> 17:32.000
Okay.

17:32.000 --> 17:36.000
Oh, by the way, darling, how old are you?

17:36.000 --> 17:37.000
Twelve years old.

17:37.000 --> 17:38.000
Twelve years old.

17:38.000 --> 17:39.000
All right, we'll play Getting to Know You.

17:39.000 --> 18:03.000
All right, we'll play Getting to Know You.

18:03.000 --> 18:23.000
All right.

18:23.000 --> 18:47.000
All right.

18:47.000 --> 19:05.000
All right.

19:05.000 --> 19:25.000
All right.

19:25.000 --> 19:45.000
All right.

19:45.000 --> 20:05.000
All right.

20:05.000 --> 20:18.000
Now, Tony, look, I don't care if we're here all night.

20:18.000 --> 20:21.000
I don't care if we go into the next show just once.

20:21.000 --> 20:25.000
I want you to play it with the right, with the counter melody.

20:25.000 --> 20:26.000
Will you please do it for me?

20:26.000 --> 20:29.000
Just as a favor, don't show off with it.

20:29.000 --> 20:31.000
Just play it straight.

20:31.000 --> 20:33.000
Twelve years old.

20:33.000 --> 20:35.000
She's 31 if she's a day.

21:04.000 --> 21:25.000
Twelve years old.

21:25.000 --> 21:34.000
Roses are red, violets are blue.

21:34.000 --> 21:35.000
I'm beginning to sound like you.

21:35.000 --> 21:38.000
Roses are red, carnations are white, and you are fired as of tonight.

21:38.000 --> 22:07.000
All right.

22:07.000 --> 22:20.000
Thank you very much, ladies and gentlemen.

22:20.000 --> 22:38.000
I hope you all enjoyed the show, and I'll be seeing you soon.

22:50.000 --> 23:15.000
Bye-bye.

